    <header class="article-header">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span></span> Tabanan Medical Emergency Guide</div>
      <h1 class="display">Food Poisoning in Tabanan? 4-Hour Emergency Protocol &amp; Villa Medical Care</h1>
      <div class="article-meta">
        <span>By Dripwell Medical Team</span> • 
        <span>September 2026</span> • 
        <span>5 min read</span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- FEATURED IMAGE -->
    <div class="featured-image-wrapper">
      <img src="https://www.dripwellbali.com/blog/food-poisoning-emergency-protocol-tabanan/tabanan-protocol-hero.jpg" alt="Emergency Doctor Visit and IV Drip for Food Poisoning in Tabanan" width="820" height="480" loading="eager" decoding="async">
    </div>

    <!-- ARTICLE BODY -->
    <div class="article-body">
      <p>
        Tabanan’s peaceful coastal villas in Kedungu and tranquil hideaways in Yeh Gangga offer a world of escape from Bali’s bustling tourist hubs[cite: 1]. However, experiencing sudden food poisoning or severe gastroenteritis in a secluded location can feel overwhelming.
      </p>

      <p>
        When acute symptoms like vomiting, abdominal spasms, and dehydration strike far from major medical facilities, taking structured immediate action is critical.
      </p>

      <div class="highlight-box">
        <p><strong>Clinical Focus:</strong> Food poisoning triggers rapid electrolyte depletion. In Tabanan’s humid climate, severe fluid loss leads to rapid circulatory fatigue within hours if left unmanaged.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>The First 4 Hours: Emergency First-Response Protocol</h2>
      <p>
        The initial four hours of onset dictate how quickly your digestive system recovers. Follow this protocol while resting in your accommodation:
      </p>

      <h3>Hour 1: Absolute Gastrointestinal Rest</h3>
      <p>
        Avoid eating food or drinking large quantities of water immediately after vomiting. Allow your stomach lining to settle for at least 45 to 60 minutes to prevent recurrent gastric contractions.
      </p>

      <h3>Hour 2: Micro-Sip Rehydration</h3>
      <p>
        Begin taking small, controlled sips (one teaspoon every 5 minutes) of oral rehydration salts or room-temperature coconut water. Avoid cold beverages or acidic juices that aggravate stomach mucosa.
      </p>

      <h3>Hour 3: Symptom Monitoring</h3>
      <p>
        Check for red-flag markers: core body fever above 38.5°C, inability to retain micro-sips, or persistent sharp abdominal cramps.
      </p>

      <h3>Hour 4: Evaluating Medical Escalation</h3>
      <p>
        If vomiting or fluid loss persists beyond 4 hours, oral absorption becomes ineffective. Professional intravenous intervention is required to restore baseline electrolyte balance directly into your bloodstream.
      </p>

      <h2>Comparison: Self-Care vs. Villa Medical Intervention</h2>

      <table class="custom-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Recovery Factor</th>
            <th>Self-Care Management</th>
            <th>On-Demand Doctor &amp; IV Drip</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Hydration Path</strong></td>
            <td>Gastrointestinal absorption (Impainred during illness)</td>
            <td>100% Systemic absorption via isotonic IV infusion</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Medication Delivery</strong></td>
            <td>Oral anti-emetics (Risk of vomiting before absorption)</td>
            <td>Direct IV administration (Rapid nausea suppression)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Travel Effort</strong></td>
            <td>Requires traveling to a clinic while weak</td>
            <td>Zero movement required (Doctor arrives at your villa)[cite: 1]</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Recovery Timeline</strong></td>
            <td>24 to 72 hours</td>
            <td>Noticeable relief within 30 to 60 minutes</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>Why Villa-Delivered Medical Care is Essential in Tabanan</h2>
      <p>
        Navigating regional traffic or searching for open pharmacies in Tabanan while suffering from acute illness causes unnecessary physical stress[cite: 1]. <strong>Dripwell Bali</strong> bridges high-end hospitality and professional clinical medicine by bringing licensed doctors and nurses directly to your villa[cite: 1].
      </p>
      <p>
        Our dedicated <strong>Bali Belly &amp; Medical Recovery Package</strong> provides:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>In-villa clinical consultation and vital sign assessment by a registered physician[cite: 1].</li>
